Short description
A quick guide to recording daily shop sales, chicken stock, expenses, and customer credit in NVSENTRY.

Video script (about 40 seconds)
[Show the Daily Entry page]
“Welcome to NVSENTRY, your daily shop ledger. Start by choosing the date for your entry.”

[Scroll through the form]
“Enter the chicken bought and chopped, closing stock, and total weight sold. Add your sales and payment amounts, then record customer counts and any expenses, credit, or supplier payments.”

[Show the opening stock fields]
“Opening stock and cash can carry forward automatically from your previous saved entry.”

[Show the Save button]
“When you’re done, select Save entry to keep your record.”

[Open Past Entries and Shop Summary]
“Use Past entries to review previous records, or Shop summary to see a daily overview.”

[Optional: show the microphone button]
“You can also try Hindi voice entry using the microphone button. Allow microphone access if your browser asks.”

[End screen]
“NVSENTRY helps you keep your shop’s daily records organized in one place.”